  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cash and Livelihoods Support_CHIAs</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Community Health and Inclusion Association (CHIAs) has worked as an officially recognised community-based organisation since 2005 and was officially registered in 2012. CHIAs is the focal point of a national network of support for people living with HIV/AIDS in Laos. CHIAs works to ensure their concerns and interests are articulated and represented at provincial, national, and regional levels. CHIAs will play a key role in the delivery of all project interventions with their provincial and district partners in Xayaburi, where they have been working for several years. They are co-facilitators for an EU-funded programme on COVID-19 response, and recently completed a study on the impact of the pandemic on marginalized groups such as LGBTI. They are currently partnering with Oxfamon a COVID-19 vaccine roll-out in southern Laos funded by AHP/DFAT. Their extensive knowledge and experience on healthcare will be essential for all partners to prepare and deliver appropriate COVID-19 health kits.

The two associations have decided to collaborate on developing common objectives, in particular those that support a world based on relationships of solidarity and greater justice. The two associations agree that respect for Human Rights, including the Rights of Women and Children, forms part of their commitment, as well as respect for Social and Economic Rights for everyone. The Action that is subject to the present agreement is a contribution towards these objectives but it cannot be considered as the sole link that unites the three associations.

The partner  CHIAsand Oxfam-in-Laos undertake to build a relationship that reinforces each party&#x2019;s work and skills, while developing each organisation&#x2019;s respective strategies.

By way of an example, CHIAs  is interested in taking part in activities that heighten awareness among the Laos public, by sending personnel and/or equipment in relation to the issue concerned by the Action. CHIAs  would also like to take part in the discussions held by the Oxfam-in-Laos onstrategic reflections connected with the action.

Oxfam undertakes to share information that may be useful for the missions of CHIAs  and to assist CHIAs  using methodological tools and supports.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As of 11 March 2020, our organization has changed our name from Lao Positive Health Association (LaoPHA) to Community Health and Inclusion Association (CHIAs), as approved by the Ministry of Home Affairs, in order to broaden our mandates and more effectively respond to broader needs of our key affected communities. Our organization mandates have been focusing on strengthening community systemto advocate for Community-Led on Health, Nutrition, Rights and Genders for key diversity population, hard to reach groups and People Living with Diseases.
The Community Health &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Inclusion Association was established under the name &#x2018;Lao Youth AIDS Project: LYAP&#x2019; in 1999 and later legally registered under the Association decree 238/PM, 2017.(Reg. No. 94/MOHA) in 2012under the name &#x2018;Lao Positive Health Association: LaoPHA&#x2019;. In 2020, the organization has rebranded itself to &#x2018;Community Health &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Inclusion Association&#x201d; to reflect our current mandates that have become more diversified, which is to strengthen the communitysystems to advocate for community-led on health, community, rights and genders of vulnerable populations and the inclusion of key populations to take care of their health and social protection effectively by partnering with government agencies and international organizations. The emphasis is on vulnerable populations, including people with sexual diversity, women and children, migrant workers, people living with diseases, ethnic minorities and people inject drugs to be aware of their health, wellbeing and rights protection including being capable of effective response and effective access to relevant government&#x2019;s services.
Our Vision:
CHIAs&#x2019;s vision is to inspire inclusive communities where all key vulnerable populations and diverse groups take leadership to ensure improved health, individual rights and gender equality.
Our missions:
- Ensure all key vulnerable populations and diverse groups and people living with diseases have effective, affordable and equitable access to healthcare, rights and socialprotection;
- Ensure gender equality and sexual rights as well aseradicate violence, human trafficking and all forms of discriminations;
- Eradicate hunger and ensure adequate nutrition for all
- Strengthen partnership for development</narrative>
